{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"The cleanup is done and up as **PR #12**: https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/12\n\nWhat it does: deletes the six pure pipe-through modules (`git.ts`, `canonical.ts`, `reanchor.ts`, `reanchor-suggest.ts`, `forge/`, `redact/apply.ts`) with everything importing `annals` directly; collapses the three namespace-binding redact wrappers into a single `src/redact.ts`; rewrites the README's \"as of 0.26.0\" changelog paragraph into a steady-state architecture note; and drops one unused re-export. What's left under `src/` is now exactly cledger: the vocabulary, the namespace binding, the adapters, and the CLI. I also deleted the retired `design/extension-governance` branch and its worktree, plus the merged `annals-extraction` branch, local and remote. Verified before pushing: 90/90 tests and the full end-to-end smoke (capture → hook install → `git push` carrying notes → log/show/export → scan) on the cleanup branch, since your live install tracks this checkout.\n\nDeliberately *not* in this PR, with what unblocks each:\n\n1. **`scripts/wipe-ev1-history.sh` and the ev1 tolerance in `fromAnnals`** — both wait on you actually running the wipe. That's the one remaining item on your plate: `sh scripts/wipe-ev1-history.sh` to preview, then `--execute`, in a plain terminal. Tell me when it's done and I'll ship the small follow-up PR that removes both.\n2. **The `ConversationRef` alias** — waits on the turnbridge agent migrating to `StreamRef`; whoever's session touches cledger next after that lands can delete it.\n3. **npm publish** — annals to npm, then cledger's `file:../annals` becomes a version range. Not started; entirely optional until you want either package installable off this machine.\n\nSo: merge PR #12 when you're happy (merge commit, as before), run the wipe, and ping me for the follow-up. Everything else from the original arc — the extraction, the envelope, the turnbridge handoff, the recursion bug — is closed out.\n\nresult: Cleanup shipped as conversation-ledger PR #12 (pipe-through modules deleted in favor of direct annals imports, redact wrappers consolidated, README made steady-state, stale branches removed; 90/90 tests + e2e smoke green) — remaining: you run the ev1 wipe script, then a small follow-up PR removes it and the ev1 read-tolerance; ConversationRef alias waits on turnbridge; npm publish optional.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"cleanup/annals-extraction-debt","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"6db8b27b11f6bb207423cc2df7e9f08e7dfe6cdb","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-9766fa946a2dbe290cdc61712a548bfed40018231a3cf9e5f396a9b9f67ceda9","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-fable-5","session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.277"},"occurred_at":"2026-09-18T22:10:55.977Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","apiBlockIndex":0,"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"cleanup/annals-extraction-debt","isSidechain":false,"message":{"container":null,"content":[{"text":"The cleanup is done and up as **PR #12**: https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/12\n\nWhat it does: deletes the six pure pipe-through modules (`git.ts`, `canonical.ts`, `reanchor.ts`, `reanchor-suggest.ts`, `forge/`, `redact/apply.ts`) with everything importing `annals` directly; collapses the three namespace-binding redact wrappers into a single `src/redact.ts`; rewrites the README's \"as of 0.26.0\" changelog paragraph into a steady-state architecture note; and drops one unused re-export. What's left under `src/` is now exactly cledger: the vocabulary, the namespace binding, the adapters, and the CLI. I also deleted the retired `design/extension-g